Derive context percent from displayed token count

The used/capacity label took its token count from total_input_tokens
while the percentage came from Claude's pre-calculated used_percentage.
Right after /compact those two sources briefly disagree (token count
still reflects the last API response while used_percentage has reset),
producing contradictions like the reported "(201k/1M) empty-bar 0%".

Compute the percentage from the same token count we display so the
label, bar, and percent always agree; fall back to used_percentage only
when no token count is available.

